      "findingMessages": {
        "p0004-schema-renamepreview-contract-claims-mutation": "The published command contract for `photo.renamePreview`, a non-journaled `query` that only returns plan_rename's plans, is copied verbatim from photo.rename. It says the command renames the files on disk (sidecars too) and is undoable. An MCP agent or UI that chooses commands from this schema text may treat the preview as the mutation: it reports files as renamed when nothing changed, or avoids calling the preview because it believes the preview is destructive.",
        "p0004-schema-placenames-undocumented-base-param": "metadata.downloadPlaceNames reads a `base` parameter (the download address, line 221) and rejects non-https values with \"`base` must be an https:// address\". Its published contract (line 286) declares only `{dataset?: folder}` and states the data comes from download.geonames.org. Schema-driven callers cannot know the parameter exists, and the contract's claim about the source is not enforced by the implementation."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "p0004-schema-renamepreview-contract-claims-mutation": "Change the description to say it returns the planned renames (`[RenamePlan]`) without touching files, and document the returned shape.",
        "p0004-schema-placenames-undocumented-base-param": "Either remove `base` from the release command surface or add it to the contract with its constraints."
      },
