            "path": "crates/engine/src/cmd/manage.rs",
            "line": 158,
            "text": "cmd!(query \"photo.renamePreview\", \"Rename Preview\", [], None, \"{template: e.g. `{date}_{name}`, `Trip-{seq:3}` (tokens: {name} {num} {seq} {seq:N} {date} {date:%Y%m%d} {folder} {camera} {lens} {iso} {rating} {title} {creator} {ext}; photo.renameTokens explains each), start?: first sequence number (1), ids?} — renames the files on disk (sidecars too, never overwriting: collisions get -1, -2…); undoable\", has_selection, |s, p| {"
          },
          "failureScenario": "The published command contract for `photo.renamePreview`, a non-journaled `query` that only returns plan_rename's plans, is copied verbatim from photo.rename. It says the command renames the files on disk (sidecars too) and is undoable. An MCP agent or UI that chooses commands from this schema text may treat the preview as the mutation: it reports files as renamed when nothing changed, or avoids calling the preview because it believes the preview is destructive.",
          "action": "Change the description to say it returns the planned renames (`[RenamePlan]`) without touching files, and document the returned shape.",
          "verifyStatus": "verified",
          "changeAttribution": {
